            <ArticleTitle>Upper body clothing is a source of fungal beta-(1,3)-glucan exposure.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>649-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Beta-(1,3)-glucan is pro-inflammatory and has been associated with airway inflammation and respiratory symptoms. This study assessed beta-(1,3)-glucan levels from upper body clothing (jerseys) of 55 subjects. Beta-(1,3)-glucan levels were estimated with a modified Limulusamoebocyte lysate kinetic assay. Beta-(1,3)-glucan levels ranged widely from 2,697 to 162,690 ng/g. Beta-(1,3)-glucan levels were significantly lower from cotton jerseys and from warm water washed jerseys. Thus, jerseys are potentially a significant exposure source of beta-(1,3)-glucan.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
